// CONFORMANCE-CASE
// spec: 15-function-semantics
// facility: rule.fn.closure [Closure-Form-Borrow], spec/14 deriv (CHG-0100); rule.value-object.write [Write-Conflict]
// kind: negative
// expect: diag.aliasing-conflict (static)
//
// A read-only capture is a live shared reference for as long as the
// closure lives; the owner may read alongside it but not write.
// Refuted statically since CHG-0100: a binding holding a closure
// without `move` carries spec/14 `deriv` facts for its captures.

fn main()
{
    i32 x = 1;
    auto f = [x]()
    {
        x
    };
    i32 y = x + f();
    x = 2;
}
